    {
      "id": "note",
      "type": "NoteNode",
      "x": -580,
      "y": -193,
      "init": {
        "label": "How it works",
        "body": "# Sudoku solver\n\nThe container is a **Simulation** loop over an 81×9 **candidate matrix** (one cell per row, one digit per column). Every matrix here is built by an **Expression** formula, the peer table and the unit table included, so there are no giant lookup grids to scroll past.\n\nEach round is one deduction pass:\n\n1. **Naked singles** — a cell pinned to one digit removes it from every peer.\n2. **Hidden singles** — a digit with one home left in a row, column or box claims that cell.\n3. **Naked pairs** — two cells sharing the same two candidates knock those digits out of any cell that sees both.\n\nCandidates only ever shrink, so the loop settles to a fixpoint well inside the configured rounds. Edit the puzzle (0 = empty), then press **Solve** on the container. *Solved* confirms every cell pinned to exactly one digit. Drill in to see the machinery."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "puzzle",
      "type": "TableInputNode",
      "x": -475,
      "y": -5,
      "init": {
        "label": "Puzzle (0 = empty)",
        "tableText": "6, 2, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 0, 9\n8, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 3, 7\n0, 0, 0, 9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1\n0, 0, 5, 8, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0\n0, 0, 9, 0, 4, 0, 6, 0, 0\n0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 5, 0, 1, 3\n0, 5, 0, 0, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0\n7, 0, 6, 0, 9, 0, 0, 2, 0\n0, 0, 0, 4, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0"
      }
    },
